## `docs/machine-factory-integration.md` — Fa-specific wording removed

Fixed. The Fa/deployment-specific parenthetical — "(self-hosted legs on the engine repo: `bash setup/dart.sh`)" — is dropped from the `DART_VERSION` row (line 88). The row now documents only the repo-agnostic machinery:

- `.dart-version` repo pin → `dart-lang/setup-dart` `sdk:`/`channel:` detection → stable with the loud may-differ-from-CI warning;
- non-Dart repos skip the install;
- `dart.sh summary` emits the `toolchain:` leg-summary line appended by `js/common/toolchainSummary.js`.

The generic preamble sentence ("Dart-repo runners add `bash agents/setup/dart.sh` to `customParams.setupCommands`") is unchanged — it predates this PR and applies to consuming repos, not to a deployment.

